  "notes": "The commemoration of the living, with the silence in which the priest names those he prays for; the missal marks it N. et N., and the edition omits the slot as it does in Te ígitur, carrying the pause as its own rubric segment. MEMÉNTO at w001 is the future imperative of memini — the only kind that verb has (meménto, plural mementóte); Whitaker's Words tags it present, Collatinus future, so the token stands as an argued divergence in the agreement report. CÓGNITA at w012 and NOTA at w015 are tagged as adjectives, with both analyzers, rather than as participles of cognósco and nosco. SE at w029 carries neither number nor gender: the reflexive marks neither, and only the case is fixed, by pro. Its provenance names Whitaker's alone beside the edition: Collatinus does not carry the bare reflexive ablative, and the token records only the analyzer that confirms it. SUÍSQUE at w030 is masculine on the persons it stands for, not on its own form.",
